 :context
 "ISIC Rev.4 5913 = motion picture/video/TV-programme DISTRIBUTION, distinct
  from sibling classes 5911 (production), 5912 (post-production), 5914
  (projection) in the same batch. Live registry.edn :name for \"5913\"
  independently re-verified fresh: truncated \"Motion picture, video and
  television programme distribution...\" (pre-existing seed-data truncation
  bug, ~10% of entries), unambiguously matching the target class and distinct
  from 5911/5912/5914's own verified names. No existing repo at
  cloud-itonami/cloud-itonami-isic-5913 (404) or at the registry's placeholder
  :repo (gftdcojp/cloud-itonami-J5913, itself bogus -- wrong org/id-shape,
  never real). Fresh scaffold, not a repair. Distribution touches
  rights/licensing-grant and territory/window-clearance decisions -- per
  ADR-2607152500's Wave4 guardrail, closed op allowlist must never include an
  op that directly finalizes either; any 'flag concern' op always escalates,
  never auto-commit-eligible."

 :scope-exclusions
 ["finalizing a rights-licensing grant (who is licensed to distribute a title, in what territory, under what terms) -- hard, permanent block"
  "finalizing a distribution-window or territory-clearance decision (locking in which window/territory a title actually releases in) -- hard, permanent block"
  "contract negotiation, minimum-guarantee/advance determination, binding distribution-agreement execution -- not represented in the closed op allowlist at all"]

 :self-trip-fix
 "Known bug class this batch repeatedly hit: bare-noun scope-excluded-terms
  (e.g. 'restraint', 'license') self-match inside the mock advisor's own
  legitimate default rationale text, self-blocking the actor's happy path.
  Fix: scope-excluded-terms phrased as the finalization/execution ACTION
  ('finalize the rights license', 'clear the distribution window', 'grant the
  license', JP equivalents), never a bare noun -- critical because
  :flag-rights-concern's entire purpose is to discuss rights/territory/
  clearance topics using exactly those bare nouns. Dedicated regression test
  default-mock-advisor-proposals-never-self-trip-scope-exclusion in
  governor_test.clj asserts all 4 default proposal generators, for a clean
  registered+verified title, never trip :scope-excluded and never HARD-hold."

 :decision
 "Implement cloud-itonami-isic-5913 with Store/Advisor/Governor/Phase/
  Operation/Sim, mirroring cloud-itonami-isic-873's eldercareops.* module
  shape module-for-module as filmdistops.*:
  - Store: Store protocol + MemStore, string-keyed titles directory
    (title-id/name/registered?/verified?), append-only ledger +
    distribution-log
  - Advisor: Advisor protocol + mock-advisor, 4 ops all :effect :propose --
    log-distribution-record, schedule-release-operation, flag-rights-concern,
    coordinate-delivery
  - Governor (FilmDistGovernor): 2 named HARD checks (title-unverified,
    effect-not-propose) + scope-exclusion/op-not-allowed folded check
    (finalize-rights-license-grant / finalize-window-territory-clearance /
    closed 4-op allowlist). always-escalate-ops #{:flag-rights-concern},
    confidence-floor 0.6
  - Phase: 0->3 rollout (phase1 = log-distribution-record only, approval;
    phase2 += schedule-release-operation/coordinate-delivery, approval;
    phase3 auto-commits those 3 when clean+confident; flag-rights-concern
    never auto, any phase)
  - Operation: real langgraph-clj StateGraph (intake->advise->govern->decide
    ->commit|hold|request-approval), interrupt-before #{:request-approval},
    NOT a stub -- mirrors eldercareops.operation exactly
  - Sim: clojure -M:run demo, full happy path + always-escalate flow + all
    HARD-hold scenarios
  - Tests: store_contract_test, advisor_test, governor_test (incl. mandatory
    self-trip regression), phase_test, governor_contract_test -- 40 tests /
    119 assertions green
  - All .cljc portable, no JVM-only interop. AGPL-3.0-or-later. README/
    GOVERNANCE/CONTRIBUTING/SECURITY/CODE_OF_CONDUCT written fresh for this
    domain (NOT copied from cloud-itonami-isic-873's own GOVERNANCE.md/
    CONTRIBUTING.md, which were found to still carry unrelated mining-actor
    (cloud-itonami-isic-0520) copy-paste boilerplate -- that bug deliberately
    not propagated here)"

